{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And I</b>. There was a scholar in Spain named ben HaYotzer, who composed a book on the End and interpreted \"a time, two times, and half a time\" as 1,550 years, their beginning from year one of Darius the Mede. He erred, for he thought this verse the words of Daniel, but it is only the words of the angel, for it is attached to what precedes. \"And none stands firm with me against these but Michael your prince\" — the meaning: just as he aided me now in my battle against the prince of Persia, so I aided him against the prince of Chaldeans, in the time of Darius the Mede the king, as it is written: \"and Darius the Mede received the kingdom,\" and this is: \"And I, in year one of Darius the Mede, stood as a support and stronghold for Michael.\" The proof that they are the words of the angel is that after it is written \"and now truth.\" One may wonder at the verse, and if a disputant says: show me its like where he broke off and returned with the word לו to the preceding passage — I have shown him: \"and YHWH appeared to him in the oaks of Mamre,\" \"and Judah approached him.\" Before I speak of the matter of Persia I shall speak of the matter of the angels, and there is no jealousy among them. And it is written: \"who makes peace in His heights.\" These are deep mysteries; none understand them but one of a thousand. I have spoken of the mystery of generations and of matters of the human soul, which is not a body, and of the wisdom of the spheres and their motion, together with matters of the planets and the constellations, and now I shall hint to you with hints, for the glory of Elohim hides the matter, and you, set your mind to discernment, and HaShem will give you wisdom." "The words of Abraham the author: Behold, na, I have prefaced regarding the One who precedes reckoning — from one aspect He is the cause of all reckoning, and from another He is all reckoning, neither increasing nor diminishing, and He is the cause of all addition and subtraction, and He accepts neither doubling nor division and is the cause of both. This One is the first world, corresponding to the worlds that come after it. This world is not a body, and it is called the vision of the glory of HaShem the Most High, and it does not change in essence or in arrangement, and it has neither time nor place, and the Name is honored within it. The second world, which is the intermediate, there are souls, true forms without bodies, also souls in bodies, and they have no number as far as we are concerned; also the bodies are as bodies, and all are honored, for they have no opposite or exchange or change in themselves, only incidentally in the arrangement of their motion. This world is called: the Hall of the Holy, and they are the heaven of heavens, and there is the Throne of Glory, and there are Michael and Gabriel. Therefore Jonathan ben Uzziel translated: \"The Holy One in the heights, the house of His Shekhinah.\" This is what he mentioned at the beginning: \"sitting upon a throne,\" and it is the Throne of Glory and its hem. The meaning: \"and the hem of the throne fills the hall.\" And he said: \"Holy in the earth, performing His might\" — these are the two concealed ones — and afterward he mentioned: \"Holy in the world of worlds.\" Know that the attribute does not change according to places; therefore the mystery of his words is: \"and he called.\" The bodies of the intermediate world neither begin nor end. And concerning this world it is written: \"Praise Him, all His angels\"; also \"His hosts,\" also \"the ministers,\" also \"the two luminaries,\" and concerning all He said: \"for He commanded and they were created,\" and \"He established them forever and ever; He gave a decree and it shall not pass.\" There is opposition in their motions: some go from east to west, and the opposite; also northward, also southward, also along the equator; also straight in their courses, also turning backward; also standing, also swift, also slow; also ascending, also descending; also appearing, also concealed; also the planets join among themselves — 120 combinations — and they, the upper ones, have no end; sometimes directly opposite, sometimes in a gaze of love. And I say: all this is only thus — through this events are renewed in the lower world, on account of their motion and their change, sometimes for good, sometimes for evil. These matters require lengthy exposition, and no single book can contain them, to know their mystery: on account of what. The third world is beneath the firmament, and it is full of bodies, thin and thick; some bodies have in them souls, also spirits, also life-forces. Man alone is the mystery of this lower world, and for his sake it was created, and his soul is bound to the upper souls. Because the one who speaks is man, and the one who hears is man, therefore the upper ones are upon man and the lower ones according to man's pattern. Behold, He is mighty over the upper ones and humbles them, for I cannot speak unless He does so, and He exalts the lower ones. Therefore the Sages said: \"The Torah spoke in the language of men.\" They say: \"and the head of the dust of the world,\" \"and it covered the eye of the earth,\" \"give ear, O earth,\" \"for the stone heard the word of YHWH,\" \"and the earth opened its mouth,\" \"from the ends of the earth in the heart of the seas,\" \"upon the bank of the river,\" \"the hand of the Jordan,\" \"wearing salvation on His head,\" \"the eyes of YHWH,\" \"in the ears of YHWH,\" \"for the mouth of YHWH has spoken,\" \"with the word of your lips,\" \"also My hand founded the earth,\" \"and My right hand spread out the heavens,\" \"and YHWH said to His heart,\" \"therefore His innards stir for Him,\" \"and beneath His feet,\" and the like; \"and the anger of YHWH burned,\" \"the lover of YHWH,\" \"and YHWH went,\" \"YHWH sat at the flood,\" \"behold, YHWH rides upon a swift cloud,\" \"awaken, why do You sleep,\" \"and He awoke as from sleep, O YHWH,\" \"I have been silent from of old,\" \"I will be still and restrain Myself.\" Behold, the prince of Persia is the one appointed over the great conjunction or the middle one. Daniel mentioned the appointed one by the name of the angel, and the word עוד is the one that is from the aspect of a gaze, which is from love, and the meaning of 21 days corresponds to the one appointed over Daniel himself, for just as there are appointees over every nation, so over every man, and the opposite of both — this is the war. This lower world is a world of reversal and exchange in essence and in arrangement and in motion, and the form that Daniel saw appeared to him in visions of prophecy. I have already revealed to you the mystery of the holy angels in brief, by way of hints, and there is proof of all this from the words of the prophets, also proofs from the external sciences. Know that decrees, both past and future, come from heaven, and they are the words of HaShem, and it is written: \"Forever, O YHWH, Your word stands firm in the heavens,\" and the mystery of the arrangements from the beginning of their creation, all the arrangements of the heavens, they are the books. Therefore the mystery of dreams. And now I return to interpret the words of the angel."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Several scriptural citations in Ibn Ezra's long catena of anthropomorphic verses are paraphrased rather than verbatim; I have translated his Hebrew renderings as they stand without identifying each source verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:20.373510433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}